# Global gitignore — proposed replacement
#
# WHAT WAS WRONG: this file was a PROJECT gitignore living in the global slot. It
# carried one project's build log, its plan files and its arXiv PDFs, plus bare
# unanchored patterns. A bare pattern like `plan.md` matches at ANY DEPTH in EVERY
# repository on this machine — so `docs/plan.md` in an unrelated repo is invisible,
# `git status` shows nothing, and the file simply does not exist to anyone else.
#
# That is not hypothetical: it is exactly how kazi-org/dira's own program plan went
# unwritten to git for the repository's entire history.
#
# WHAT CHANGED: the project-specific lines are removed (they belong in the project
# that owns them). What remains is anchored with a leading slash where it should only
# match at a repository root, so nothing matches at arbitrary depth by accident.
#
# Apply with:
#   cp docs/proposed/gitignore.global ~/.gitignore
#   git config --global core.excludesfile ~/.gitignore
#
# Then, in any repo that was relying on the old behaviour, check nothing you wanted
# tracked is newly visible or newly ignored:
#   git status --short
#   git check-ignore -v <path>     # names the file and line that ignored something

# --- safe unanchored: you never want these tracked at ANY depth ---
# .claude is deliberate and is the one entry here that is not OS noise: skills are
# global-only on this machine, so a project-local .claude is never source. It is the
# only thing the old file was ignoring in dira, and that was correct.
.DS_Store
.claude
.env
.env.local
.idea
.salt

# --- REMOVED, because they belong to a specific project, not to every repo ---
# Move these into that project's own .gitignore:
#   2004.00574v1.md
#   2004.00574v1.pdf
#   2506.21734v3.md
#   2506.21734v3.pdf
#   30day.md
#   GEMINI.md
#   artifacts
#   bin
#   bin/
#   bin/zerfoo-predict
#   bugs.md
#   coverage/junit.xml
#   gemma-plan.md
#   gemma.md
#   issues.md
#   model_data
#   plan.done.md
#   plan.md
#   plan.md
#   predictions.csv
#   predictions_metadata.json
#   tmp
#   todos.md
#   vendor
#   zonnx-converter.log

# --- if you still want any of the above globally, anchor it ---
# /plan.md          matches only a plan.md at a repository root
# plan.md           matches docs/plan.md, src/plan.md, anything — this is the trap
